 4. Run the reviewed command without `--dry-run`. Fresh groups retain `_plan.json` (bench/target/implementation hashes, Node/package/available CLI versions, allowlisted configured model settings, declared workspace paths and call budget), `_calls.jsonl` (append-only started/finished/failed events with prompt hashes), `_session.json` (completion/stop reason), and `_artifacts.json` (regular-file hashes and unfollowed symlink targets). Calibration also retains `_calibration.json` with task counts. Existing groups are never overwritten.
 5. Generate a portable report: `skillfit report eval runs/<group>/manifest.json`. Inspect task checks, errors, token coverage, read observations and session completeness before deciding. Partial/stopped sessions produce no installation recommendation even if their surviving subset favors treatment. Preserve their receipts, then fix the cause and predeclare a fresh run. Do not pool adaptive calibration into validation.
 
-Before and after each model/judge call, the harness checks pinned input bytes and matrix-listed user configuration/Skill roots. Executor failures or detected drift stop further actual calls. Returned output/transcripts are retained when a post-call check detects drift, but the trial is ungraded. Only pure project-trust registrations for predeclared disposable workspaces are excluded from the configuration hash, along with final blank newline separators; other fields, paths, trust values and bytes remain covered. Input symlinks are rejected; top-level global Skill directory aliases are pinned through their resolved content plus a watched inventory.
+Before and after each model/judge call, the harness checks pinned input bytes and matrix-listed user configuration/Skill roots. Executor failures or detected drift stop further actual calls. Returned output/transcripts are retained when a post-call check detects drift, but the trial is ungraded. Only pure project-trust registrations for predeclared disposable workspaces are excluded from the configuration hash, along with final blank newline separators; other fields, paths, trust values and bytes remain covered. Plans freeze each workspace's logical and physical path: pure trust registrations for either name are allowed, while alias retargeting stops further calls. Input symlinks are rejected; top-level global Skill directory aliases are pinned through their resolved content plus a watched inventory.
 
 This is an inspection contract, not environment isolation or tamper-proof attestation. API configured model names and allowlisted CLI settings do not prove which server model served a response. Inherited plugins, unlisted paths, toolchains, server-side drift and sampling remain uncontrolled. Judge sandbox paths are temporary and not exempted from trust checks; a new unplanned trust registration stops the run. Only the selected primary agent's matrix configuration is fingerprinted; a different judge's environment remains unrecorded. Do not include raw configuration, auth files or credentials in published artifacts. Paths and agent output may still contain private project material; inspect them before sharing.
 
